    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0373" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BE/9–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-08T19:00:00+01:00">September 8,
                            1949—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3620. Substance of Deptel 3194 September
                        2<anchor n="1" xml:id="d241-f1"/> discussed with both Jebb<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d241-f2"/> and Allen, head UN Political Department. They indicated
                    Special Committee on Information considered unnecessary and in some respects
                    even harmful. However, they promised review of British position and held out
                    some hope of modification particularly in view of point that existence of SCI had bearing on US non-participation in American
                    Committee on DA held at Havana.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 3620. Department pass USUN New
                    York unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d241-f1" n="1" xml:id="d241-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 3286, to Paris, September 2, <ref target="#pg354">p. 354</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d241-f2" n="2" xml:id="d241-f2-content">
                <p>Sir H. M. Gladwyn Jebb, Supervising Under-Secretary, United Nations Department
                    (Political, Economic, and Social), British Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
